    "lesson": {
      "title": "Galvanic cell & Nernst potential",
      "instruction": "Vary zinc and copper ion concentrations. Observe how cell voltage shifts relative to the standard 1.10 V Daniell cell according to the Nernst equation.",
      "explanation": "Standard cell potential is E° = +1.10 V (Cu²⁺/Cu = +0.34 V, Zn²⁺/Zn = -0.76 V). The Nernst equation E_cell = E° - (RT/2F)*ln([Zn²⁺]/[Cu²⁺]) shows that increasing reactant [Cu²⁺] raises voltage, while increasing product [Zn²⁺] lowers voltage."
    },
